{"id": "P08310", "name": "Roy Mann", "name_chinese": "Roy Mann", "country": "Israel", "net_worth_usd_m": "969.8", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time (former)", "source_of_wealth": "software", "industry": "technology", "sec_insider_companies": "monday.com Ltd. (MNDY) - Co-CEO", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (former) (2025); Forbes annual (2024-2025); Hurun Global (2022-2025); SEC insider holdings (2026); Hurun Unicorn founders (2019-2020)", "focus": [], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/roy-mann/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Roy Mann cofounded monday.com, a cloud-based platform that allows companies to create their own work management tools, in 2012.", "Mann, an Israeli, is co-CEO of the Tel Aviv-based company, which went public on the NASDAQ in 2021.", "Mann served as a senior tech leader at Wix.com, an Israeli provider of cloud-based web development tools, from 2010 to 2012. Wix IPO'd in 2013.", "A serial entrepreneur, Mann cofounded two other companies before joining Wix: Facebook app Save An Alien and digital marketing firm ntt.co.il."], "forbes_facts": ["Originally called dapulse, monday.com adopted its current name in 2017, as a nod to its international audience (work weeks start on Sundays in Israel).", "Zoom and Salesforce both invested in monday.com in a private placement as part of the company's IPO in 2021."]}
